hadiths[295]{hadithnumber,text}:
"129","The Prophet (ﷺ) sent me on some errands and I became junub (sexually impure), and could not find water. I rolled myself in the dirt just as an animal does. I then came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and mentioned that to him. He said, \This would have been enough for you","\"" and he struck the earth with his hands once"," then he wiped the right hand with the left one"," and the outside of the palms of his hands and his face.\n[Agreed upon. The wording is that of Muslim's]."""
"130","Allah’s Messenger (ﷺ) said: \Tayammum is two strikes: one for the face and one for the hands up to the elbows.\""\nReported by Ad-Daraqutni"""
"131","Allah’s Messenger (ﷺ) said: \The soil is a purifier for a Muslim"," even if he does not find water for ten years; but if he finds water"," he must fear Allah and let it touch his skin.\"""""
"132","Narrated Abu Dharr (RAA):a similar Hadith transmitted by at-Tirmidhi وَلِلتِّرْمِذِيِّ: عَنْ أَبِي ذَرٍّ نَحْوُهُ, وَصَحَّحَه ُ 1 .1 - صحيح. رواه الترمذي (124) ولفظه: \إن الصعيد الطيب طهور المسلم، وإن لم يجد الماء عشر سنين، فإذا وجد الماء فليمسه بشرته؛ فإن ذلك خير\"" وقال: \""حديث حسن صحيح\""."""
"133","Two men set out on a journey and when the time of Salat (prayer) came they had no water. They performed Tayammum with clean earth and prayed. Later on they found water within the time of the prayer. One of them repeated his prayer with ablution but the other did not repeat. Then they came to Allah's Messenger (ﷺ), and related the matter to him. Addressing himself to the one who did not repeat, he said, \You followed the Sunnah and your (first) prayer was enough for you.\""[9] He said to the one who performed ablution and repeated: \""For you there is a double reward\"".\n[Reported by Abu Dawud and An-Nasa'i]"""
"134","concerning the verse, “And if you are ill or on a journey...” (an-Nisa': 43). He said, \If a man sustains a wound"," which he suffered during Jihad (in the cause of Allah) or ulcers"," then he became junub (sexually impure) and is afraid that if he bathes he would die; he may perform ablution with clean earth (Tayammum).\n[Reported by Ad- Daraqutni in a Mawquf (untraceable) Hadith and Al-Bazzar in a Marfu' (traceable) one. Ibn Khuzaima and Al-Hakim graded it Sahih (sound)]."""
"135","One of my forearms was broken. Then I consulted Allah's Messenger (Peace be upon him) and he ordered me to wipe over the bandages.\n[Reported by Ibn Majah with a very weak chain of narrators]."
"136","concerning the man who had a head injury, and then he made Ghusl and died: Allah's Messenger Peace be upon him said, \It would have been enough for him to perform Tayammum and wrap it with something and wipe over the wrapping and wash the rest of his body.\""\n[Reported by Abu Da'ud"," but there is a weakness in its chain of narrators]"""
"137","It is from the Sunnah of the Prophet (ﷺ) for the man to pray only one prayer with each Tayammum, and then perform Tayammum for the next prayer.\n[Reported by Ad-Daraqutni but with a very weak chain of narrators]"
"138","Fatima bint Abu Hubaish used to have a prolonged flow of blood (Istihadah) and so Allah’s Messenger (Peace be upon him)· told her, \If it is the blood of menstruation it will be dark (almost black) and recognizable (by women). If it is that"," then leave the prayer. If it is other than that"," then make ablution and pray.\""\n[Reported by Abu Da'ud and An-Nasa’i. Ibn Hibban and Al-Hakim graded it Sahih (sound).]"""
"139","Allah’s Messenger (ﷺ) said: “Whoever performs ablution on Friday has done a good thing and he who takes bath, taking bath is better  (for him).” "," and if she sees yellowness appearing (on top of the water) she should wash (three times)"," once for the Dhuhr and Asr prayers"," and once for the Maghrib and Isha prayers"," and once for the Fajr prayer"," and she should then perform ablution in between those times.\"""""
"140","'I had a very strong prolonged flow of blood. I went to the Prophet (Peace be upon him) to ask him about it. He said, \This is a strike from Satan. So observe your menses for six or seven days"," then perform Ghusl until you see that you are clean. Pray for twenty-four or twenty-three nights and days and fast"," and that will suffice you. Do so every month just as the other women menstruate (and are purified). But if you are strong enough to delay the Dhuhr prayer and advance the Asr prayer"," then make Ghusl when your purified and combine the Dhuhr and the Asr prayers together; then delay the Maghrib prayer and advance the Isha prayer"," and perform Ghusl and combine the two prayers"," do so. Do so"," and then wash at dawn and pray Fajr. This is how you may pray and fast if you have the ability to do so.\"" And he said"," \""That is the more preferable way to me.\""\n[Reported by the five imams except An- Nasa’i"," At-Tirmidhi graded it Sahih (sound)]"""
"141","Umm Habiba bint Jahsh complained to Allah's Messenger (Peace be upon him) about a prolonged flow of blood. He said to her, \Keep away (from prayer) as long as your normal period used to prevent you (from praying)"," and afterwards she should perform Ghusl (and pray)\"". (She used to take a bath for every prayer).\n[Reported by Muslim.]"""
"142","\And perform ablution for every Salat (prayer)\"". Abu Dawud and others transmitted a similar narration."""
"143","After we were pure, we did not consider the yellow or muddy discharge to be anything (i.e. of the menses blood)\n[Reported by Al-Bukhari and Abu Dawud and the wording is of Abu Dawud]."
"144","The Jews used not to eat with a woman during her menstruation period, so the Prophet (Peace be upon him) said: \Do every thing else apart from sexual intercourse (with your wives)\"".\n[Reported by Muslim.]"""
"145","When I was menstruating, the Prophet saws would order me to wrap myself up (with an Izar, which is a dress worn below the waist) and would start fondling me.\nReported by Al-Bukhari and Muslim."
"146","Allah's Messenger (Peace be upon him) said regarding a husband who has sexual intercourse with his wife during her menstruation period, \He must pay a Dinar or half a Dinar in way of charity.”\n[Reported by the five Imams. Al-Hakim and Ibn Al-Qattan graded it Sahih (sound).]"""
"147","Allah's Messenger (Peace be upon him) said: \Is it not the case that when a woman menstruates"," she neither prays nor fasts?\""[12]\n[Reported by Al-Bukhari and Muslim. It is part of a long Hadith]"""
"148","When we came to a place called Sarif, I menstruated and the Prophet (Peace be upon him) told me, \You should perform all that a pilgrim would do"," except circumambulation until you are pure (i.e. performed Ghusl).\""\n[Reported by Al-Bukhari and Muslim and it is part of a long Hadith.]"""
"149","He asked the Prophet (Peace be upon him), “What is lawful for a man regarding his wife when she is menstruating?\ and he replied"," \""What is above the waist wrapper (Izar).”[13]\n[Reported by Abu Da'ud and graded it Da'if.]"""
"150","During the lifetime of the Prophet (Peace be upon him) the women having bleeding after delivery (postnatal or puerperal blood) would refrain (from prayer) for forty days.\n[Reported by Al-Khamsa except An-Nasa’i, and the version is that of Abu Da’ud]."
"151","It was narrated from Hazrat Abdullah bin Umar and Hazrat Aisha that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Surely, Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him) calls the call to prayer at night. You people eat and drink until the call to prayer of Ibn Umm Maktoum (RA).\ Hadhrat Ibn Umm Maktoum (RA) was a blind man"," he would not call the call to prayer until people told him that it was dawn. (Bukhari and Muslim - there is a word written at the end of it.)"""
"152","It was narrated on the authority of Hazrat Abdullah bin Umar that (one day) Hazrat Bilal recited the Adhan before dawn, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him to go again and proclaim: “Beware! Indeed, the servant had fallen asleep."
"153","It is narrated from Hazrat Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \When you hear the call to prayer"," say it in the same way as the muezzin is saying it.\"" (Bukhari and Muslim). And Muslim narrated a hadith from Hazrat Umar"," which is about the virtue of saying one word in the same way in response to the muezzin"," except for haiyy ali salaat and haiyy ali al-falah"," that instead of these words"," say la hawla wa quwa illa bilallah."""
"154","On the authority of Hazrat Uthman bin Abi Al-Aas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: O Messenger of Allah! Appoint me as the Imam of my people. He said: \You are their imam. Make the weakest among them your example and appoint a muezzin who does not take a wage for calling the call to prayer.\"""""
"155","Hazrat Malik bin Hawairat (RA) narrated that the Prophet (PBUH) said to us: \When the time for prayer comes"," one of you should call the Adhan for you.\"" Then he narrated the entire hadith. (It has been narrated by all seven)."""
"156","It is narrated from Hazrat Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Hazrat Bilal, may Allah be pleased with him: \When you say the adhan"," say it slowly"," and when you say the takbeer"," say it quickly.\"" Leave enough time between the Adhan and the Iqamah that the person eating is finished with his food (so that he can participate in the congregation).” Then he narrated the entire hadith. (Tirmidhi narrated it and declared it weak.) And in Tirmidhi it was narrated from Hazrat Abu Huraira that the Prophet"," may God bless him and grant him peace"," said: “No one should say the Adhan except a person who is ablution.” It has been declared as weak.) And in the narration of Hazrat Abdullah Bin Zayd Radiyallahu Anhu in Abu Dawud"," it is said that I saw it in a dream"," meaning the call to prayer"," and I wished to be appointed as a muezzin. He said: \""You say Takbeer.\"""""
"157","It is narrated from Hazrat Abu Huraira, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \The muezzin has more right to call the call to prayer and the imam has more right to say Takbeer.\"""""
"158","On the authority of Hazrat Anas bin Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \The prayer is not rejected in the interval between the Adhan and Iqamah.\"""""
"159","On the authority of Hazrat Jabir, the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever makes this supplication after hearing the Adhan, my intercession will be necessary for him on the Day of Resurrection: O Lord of this perfect supplication and everlasting prayer! Grant Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) means and virtue and grant him the position of Mahmud that You have promised him.” (Narrated by all four)."
"160","On the authority of Hazrat Ali bin Talaq, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \During the prayer"," when one of you passes out"," he should go back"," perform ablution again"," and perform the prayer again.\"""""
"161","Hazrat Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: “Allah does not accept the prayer of an adult woman without a turban."
"162","Hazrat Jabir (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said to him: \When the cloth is large and loose"," wrap it around the body in prayer.\"" And in the tradition of Muslim"," it is: \""(If the cloth is wide) put the two edges of the cloth on opposite shoulders.\"" And if the cloth is tight"," tie it in the form of an apron.\"" (Bukhari and Muslim) And in Bukhari and Muslim it was narrated from Hazrat Abu Huraira that \""None of you should pray in a cloth (in such a way) that no part of that cloth is on his shoulder.\"""""
"163","Hazrat Umm Salama (RA) narrated that I asked the Prophet (PBUH): Can a woman pray in just a shirt and a veil without an apron? He said: \When the shirt is so long and loose that it reaches the upper parts of the feet"," it is permissible.\"""""
"164","Hazrat Aamir bin Rabi'ah (RA) narrates that we were with the Prophet (PBUH) on a dark night and it became difficult for us to identify the direction of the qiblah. We prayed (by determining the direction of Qibla). When the sun rose, it became known that we had prayed towards the non-qibla, so (on that occasion) this verse was revealed: ﴾Fainama tuwalwa fatham wajhu Allah﴾ So wherever you turn, that is the face of Allah."
"165","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Hurairah, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \The Qiblah is between the East and the West.\"""""
"166","Hazrat Aamir bin Rabi'ah (RA) says: \I saw the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) praying on his camel"," wherever it would lead him.\"" (Bukhari and Muslim) and Bukhari has also quoted this addition that he used to point his blessed head (in prayer) and did not do so in the obligatory prayer. And it was narrated in Abu Dawud on the authority of Hazrat Anas (RA) that when he was traveling and wanted to perform the Naful prayer"," he would (once) turn his camel towards the Qiblah and say Takbeer. (The chain of this hadith is Hasan)."""
"167","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \The whole land is a mosque except for the graveyard and the bath.\"" (Pray wherever you want)."""
"168","Hazrat Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him) forbade praying in seven places: Ghare (garbage), slaughterhouses, graveyards, public streets, baths, enclosures (camel tying places) and on the roof of Baitullah. (It was narrated by Tirmidhi and called it weak.)"
"169","Hazrat Abu Murshad Ghanwi (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: “Neither pray facing the graves nor sit on them.” (Narrated by Muslim)."
"170","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When one of you comes to the mosque, he should look at (his shoes) (before entering the mosque). If there is any dirt or unclean thing in the shoes, then he should clean them and pray in them."
"171","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Huraira, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “When one of you treads dirt with his socks, the soil will purify him.”"
"172","Hazrat Mu'awiya bin Huqam (RA) narrated that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \Indeed"," there is no room for human conversation in prayer.\"" In prayer"," there should be only Tasbih (Glory be to Allah)"," Takbeer (Allahu Akbar) and recitation of the Qur’an.” (Narrated by Muslim)."""
"173","Hazrat Zayd bin Arqam, may God be pleased with him, narrates that during the blessed era of the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, we used to talk to each other during prayer and explain our needs and wants to each other until this verse was revealed: Protect the prayers and especially the middle prayer (Asr). And stand in silence in front of Allah.\ So we were ordered to remain silent and forbidden to talk and speak in prayer. (Bukhari and Muslim - these words are from Muslim)."""
"174","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “For men, it is tasbih (informing the imam in prayer by saying Subhaan Allah) and for women, clapping their hands.” (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"175","Hazrat Mutaraf, may God have mercy on him, narrates from his father, Abdullah bin Shukhair, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, praying. (It has been narrated by all five except Ibn Majah, and Ibn Hibban has declared it Sahih.)"
"176","It was narrated from Hazrat Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) that I had two occasions to attend the service of the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him). When I was in your service and you were praying, you would call to inform me. (Narrated by Nisai and Ibn Majah.)"
"177","Hazrat Ibn Umar Radiyallahu Anhu narrates that I asked Hazrat Bilal Radiyallahu Anhu: How did you see the Prophet (Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam) replying when he was praying and people greeted him? He said you would do it like this. And stretched out his hand. (Narrated by Abu Dawud and Tirmidhi, and Tirmidhi declared it Sahih.)"
"178","It was narrated on the authority of Hazrat Abu Qatadah that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to carry (his granddaughter) Imama bint Zaynab while leading the prayer. When you went into prostration, you used to put it down, and when you stood up after prostrating, you would pick it up (again). (Bukhari and Muslim) and there is this addition in Muslim: You used to lead the people in the mosque."
"179","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Hurairah, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Kill two black animals in prayer: a snake and a scorpion.\"""""
"180","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Juhaim bin Harith, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “If one who passes in front of a person in prayer knows how much of a sin it is to do so (passing in front of a person in prayer), he would prefer to stand there for forty (years) than to pass in front of the person in prayer.” (Bukhari and Muslim) These words are Bukhari’s. It is mentioned."
"181","It is narrated from Hazrat Aisha (RA) that on the occasion of the Battle of Tabuk, the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) was asked about the length of a prayer stick (how long should it be?) and he said: \It should be equal to the height of the wood at the back of a camel's bed.\"" (Narrated by Muslim)."""
"182","On the authority of Hazrat Sabra bin Mubad Al-Juhani, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Each one of you should set up seven times when performing the prayer"," even if it is only an arrow.\"" (Narrated by Al-Hakim)."""
"183","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Dharr, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \A Muslim man's prayer is broken by a woman"," a donkey"," and a black dog"," unless there are seventeen in front of him equal to the back of the crib.\"" This is a long hadith. It also mentions these words: \""A black dog is Satan.\"" (Narrated by Muslim.) And in Muslim"," there is a similar narration of Hazrat Abu Huraira"," but there is no mention of a dog in it. Also"," Abu Dawood and Nasa'i have also quoted the same from Hazrat Ibn Abbas"," but the last part of the hadith is not in it. And the confinement and condition of becoming an adult has also been mentioned."""
"184","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \When one of you begins to pray after establishing the prayer"," and a man starts to pass in front of him (between the prayer and the prayer)"," he (the person praying) should try to stop him.\"" If he (the passer-by still) does not stop"," then fight him because he is Satan (in human form).” (Bukhari and Muslim) And in one hadith: “He has a companion (Satan) with him.”"""
"185","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Huraira, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \When one of you begins to pray"," he should place something in front of his face.\"" If something is not available"," then just set up your stick. If even a stick is not possible"," then draw a line (on the ground). Now the passer-by will not be able to harm him.” (It has been narrated by Ahmad and Ibn Majah and Ibn Hibban has declared it to be Sahih"," and whoever thinks that this hadith is mutzarab"," he has not said it is Sahih (he is in error)"," but it is a good hadith.)"""
"186","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Saeed al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Nothing breaks the prayer"," and try to stop (the object passing in front of you) as much as possible.\"""""
"187","It is narrated from Hazrat Abu Huraira that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade praying with hands on the sides. (Bukhari and Muslim - these words are from Muslim.) And the meaning of this (briefly) is that the person praying should keep his hands on his side. And in Bukhari, it was narrated from Hazrat Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that \This is the way (of prayer) of the Jews.\"""""
"188","On the authority of Hazrat Anas, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \When the evening meal has been served"," eat before offering the Maghrib prayer.\"" (Bukhari and Muslim)"""
"189","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Dharr, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When one of you is praying, do not remove the stones (pebbles) from his hand (from the place of worship), because (at that time) the mercy of God is directed towards him.” (Narrated by all five with a valid chain of transmission.) Musnad Ahmad has this addition: (If the pebbles are to be removed), “remove them once or leave them.” And Sahih Bukhari. I have narrated the same tradition from Hazrat Muayqib, but the reason is not mentioned in it."
"190","Hazrat Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated that I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about looking around during the prayer, and he said: “This is a trick by which Satan steals a part of a person’s prayer.” However, due to severe and unavoidable compulsion, this can be done in Nawafil."
"191","Hazrat Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “When one of you is in prayer, he is whispering to his Lord.” So (in such a situation) do not spit in front of you and on your right side, but on your left side under your feet.” (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"192","It was narrated from Anas (RA) that Hazrat Aisha (RA) had an ornamental cloak which she hung on one side of her room. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them: \Remove this decorative cloak of yours from before us"," because its patterns and designs have been constantly appearing before me in my prayers.\"" And in it is: \""This cloak made me forget my prayer.\"""""
"193","It was narrated from Hazrat Jabir bin Samurah that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “People must refrain from raising their eyes towards the sky in prayer, lest their eyes return (to become blind).” (Narrated by Muslim). You are pushing stool."
"194","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Huraira, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Yawning is an evil act.\"" If anyone among you yawns"," he should try to stop it as much as possible.\"" (Narrated by Muslim and Tirmidhi"," and Tirmidhi has quoted the addition of \""in Namaz (yawning)\"" in his narration.)"""
"195","On the authority of Hazrat Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered the construction of mosques in the villages and that they should be kept clean and scented. (It was narrated by Ahmad, Abu Dawud and Tirmidhi, and Tirmidhi declared its transmission to be authentic.)"
"196","It is narrated from Hazrat Abu Huraira, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \May Allah destroy the Jews. They made the graves of the prophets a place of prostration.\"" (Bukhari and Muslim) Muslim also quoted the addition of the word \""Nasari\"". There are also: \""These are the worst creatures.\"""""
"197","It was narrated from Hazrat Abu Huraira that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a troop of horsemen. These people arrested a man and brought him to your service and tied him to one of the pillars of the (Prophetic) Mosque. This is a long hadith. (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"198","It was narrated on the authority of Hazrat Abu Huraira that Hazrat Omar passed by Hazrat Hasan while he was reciting poetry in the mosque. Hazrat Umar looked at him. (On this) Hazrat Hasan (RA) said: (Why are you staring?) I used to recite poetry in the mosque, while there was that beloved person in the mosque who was better than you, i.e. the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"199","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Huraira, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Whoever hears a man announcing a lost thing in the mosque"," then say to him"," May God grant that you do not find that thing back.\"" Mosques were not built for this purpose. (Narrated by Muslim.)"""
"200","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Huraira, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \When you see a person buying and selling in the mosque"," say to him: May Allah not give you profit in your business and trade.\"""""
"201","On the authority of Hazrat Hakeem bin Hizam, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There should be no limits in the mosques, nor should qisas (blood revenge) be taken in them.”"
"202","Hazrat Aisha (RA) narrates that Hazrat Sa'd (RA) was injured on the day of Ghazwa Khandaq, so the Messenger of Allah (SAW) pitched a tent for him in the mosque so that he could be closely nursed (easily). (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"203","It was narrated from Hazrat Aisha that I saw the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he was a veil for me and I was looking at the Abyssinians who were playing in the mosque. This is a long hadith. (Bukhari and Muslim)."
"204","It was narrated from Hazrat Aisha that a black girl had a tent in the mosque. She used to come to me to talk. This is a long hadith. (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"205","On the authority of Hazrat Anas, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Spitting in the mosque is a sin"," and its expiation is to bury the spit.\"" (Bukhari and Muslim)."""
"206","Hazrat Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “The Hour will not be established (until that time) until people are proud of each other in (building) mosques.”"
"207","Hazrat Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “I was not ordered to decorate the mosques and plaster them.”"
"208","On the authority of Hazrat Anas, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I was presented with the rewards (and good deeds) of my ummah, even the straw that a man throws out of the mosque (this was also among the good deeds.”)"
"209","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Qatada, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Whenever any of you enters the mosque"," he should not sit without praying two rak'ahs.\"" (Bukhari and Muslim)."""
"210","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Huraira, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \When you intend to stand up for prayer"," first perform ablution well"," then face the Qibla and say Takbeer (Allahu Akbar)","\"" then recite the part of the Qur'an that you can recite easily. Then bow down and bow down with full satisfaction"," then raise your head (from bowing) and stand up with full satisfaction. Then prostrate and prostrate with complete satisfaction"," then raise your head from prostration and sit with complete satisfaction. Then perform the second prostration and perform prostration with complete satisfaction. Then in all your (remaining) prayers"," do it in the same way (perform the parts of prayer with satisfaction).'' And it is in a tradition of Musnad Ahmad: “Straighten your back (back) until the bones return (to their place).” Narrated by Rafa’ah bin Rafi’ (may God be pleased with him) in Nasa’i and Abu Dawud: “None of you can complete his prayer until he completes ablution (in the same way) as Allah has commanded him","” then says Takbeer and praises Allah.” And this is also mentioned in this tradition. It is: \""If you remember any part of the Qur'an"," then recite it.\"" Otherwise"," recite Alhamdulillah"," Allah Akbar and La ilaha illa Allah.\"" In Abu Dawud"," it is: \""Then recite Surah Al-Fatiha and more as Allah wills.\"" And in Ibn Hibban"," it is: \""Then (read) whatever you want."""
"211","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Hameed Sa'idi, may Allah be pleased with him, he states that I saw that when the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, would say the Takbeer, he would raise both his hands to the level of his shoulders, and when bowing, he would hold his knees firmly with both hands, then he would bow his back, and then when he raised his head from bowing, he would stand straight in such a way that each joint would return to its proper place. Then (after that) when he would prostrate, he would place both his hands (on the ground) in such a way that (the arms) were lying on the ground and not bent (towards the sides). And you (in prostration) would turn the toes of your two feet towards the Qiblah. And when you would sit after reading two rak'ahs, you would sit on your left foot and keep your right foot standing. And when he would sit in the last rak'at, he would extend his left foot (from under the right thigh) and keep his right foot upright and sit on the saddle. (Narrated by Bukhari.)"
"212","It was narrated from Hazrat Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) that when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would stand up for prayer, he would (first) recite this supplication: [Wajhtu wajhi lil-dhi fattar al-samawaat wa al-arza] from [minna al-muslimeen]. (Then they would read:) [Allah, I am the master, there is no god, I am your Lord, and I am your slave] until the end. (Narrated by Muslim.) And it is in a tradition of Muslim that he used to recite this in the night prayer (Tahjud)."
"213","It was narrated from Hazrat Abu Hurairah that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to remain silent for a while after reciting the Takbeer and then start reciting it. (One day) I asked him about it (O Messenger of Allah! What do you read during the break?) He said: “I [Allah! I read after my mistakes... O Allah! Put as much distance between me and my sins as the distance between east and west. O Allah! Cleanse me from sins and mistakes like a white cloth is cleaned from dirt. O Allah! Wash me from my sins with water, snow and hail.” (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"214","Hazrat Umar (RA) used to read (during the interval): [Subhanak Allahum wa bihamdik...etc.] “O Allah! Thou art pure (from every blemish and every imperfection.) All praises are due to Thee. Blessed is your name and exalted is your glory. And there is no god but You.'' He used to recite al-Rajīm from Hamzah and Nafkhīh and Nafthīh). \I seek refuge in Allah"," the All-Knowing"," from Satan the Rejected"," from his whispers"," from his blowing"," that is"," from pride and arrogance"," and from his poetry and magic.\"""""
"215","It is narrated from Hazrat Aisha that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to start his prayer with Allahu Akbar and recite Qirata al-Hamdu Lillah Rabbi’ al-Alameen (Surah Al-Fatihah). And when bowing, he would not raise his blessed head, nor would he lower it too low, but would place it in the middle of it. And when he raised his head from bowing, he would not prostrate until he stood up straight. And when he raised his head from prostration, he would not perform the second prostration until he sat down in the correct manner. And after every two rak'ahs, he would read Tashhud and put his left foot on the ground and keep his right foot upright. And he used to forbid sitting with arms spread like the shaytan's foursome and beasts. And used to end the prayer with salam. (It was narrated by Muslim and its chain of transmission is valid.)"
"216","It was narrated from Hazrat Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) that when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began the prayer, he would raise both his hands up to the level of his shoulders, and when he bowed he would say Allahu Akbar and when he raised his head from bowing (even then he would perform Rifa-ul-Ideen in the same way). (Bukhari and Muslim) and in Abu Dawud, on the authority of Hazrat Abu Hamid, may Allah be pleased with him, in a hadith, that he would raise both his hands until they reached the level of his shoulders, then say Allahu Akbar. And it is narrated in Muslim on the authority of Hazrat Malik bin Hawairat (RA) like the narration of Hazrat Ibn Umar (RA), but it says that he used to raise it up to the top of his ears."
"217","Hazrat Wail bin Hajar (RA) narrates that I prayed with the Prophet (PBUH), he placed his right hand on his left hand and tied both hands on his chest."
"218","Narrated by Hazrat Ubada bin Samit, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \There is no prayer for a person who does not recite Umm Al-Qur'an (in prayer).\"" (Bukhari and Muslim) It is narrated in Ibn Hibban and Darqutani: \""The prayer in which Surah Al-Fatihah is not recited is not sufficient.\"" Yes?'' We said: 'Yes.'"""
"219","It was narrated from Anas (RA) that the Prophet (PBUH), Abu Bakr (RA) and Umar (RA) used to start their prayers with [Al-Hamdu-Lillah-Rabbi-ul-Alameen]. (Bukhari and Muslim). In a tradition of Musnad Ahmad' Nasa'i and Ibn Khuzimah: They did not recite [Bism-i-Allah-ir-Rahman-ir-Raheem] aloud. In another tradition of Ibn Khuzimah: He used to recite Bismillah slowly. And the negation of Sahih Muslim's tradition will be attributed to him, unlike those who have called it Maaloool."
"220","Hazrat Naeem Mujmar (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated that I prayed under the leadership of Hazrat Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) and he first recited in the name of Allah, then recited Umm Al-Qur’an (Surah Al-Fatiha) and even when he reached (Wal-al-Dha’aleen) he said Amen. And whenever he prostrated and whenever he stood up after sitting, he would say Allahu Akbar. Then he returned the salutation and said: I swear by the One in Whose hand is my life! Indeed, I am the most similar to you with the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace. (My prayer is very similar to the prayer of the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace.) (Narrated by Nasa'i and Ibn Khuzima)."
"221","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When you recite Surah Al-Fatiha, recite Bismillah, Rahman al-Raheem, because it is also a verse of Surah Al-Fatihah.”"
"222","It was narrated from Hazrat Abu Huraira that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished reciting Umm al-Qur'an (Surah Al-Fatiha), he would say Amen in a loud voice. (It has been narrated by Darqutani and called it hasan. And it has been narrated by Al-Hakim and has been declared authentic. Also, the narration of Hazrat Wail bin Hajar (RA) is similar in Abu Dawud and Tirmidhi.)"
"223","It was narrated on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Ufa (may Allah be pleased with him) that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said, \I cannot remember anything from the Qur'an"," so teach me something that will suffice (for my prayer) in its place.\"" He said: \""Glory be to God"," and praise be to God"," and there is no god but God"," and God is great.\"" Al-Azeem] \""Allah is pure\"" He is praised \""There is no god but He\"" and Allah is the Greatest \""Aversion from evil and success of good deeds\"" is not possible with anyone but Allah.\"" Read it.\"" It is a long hadith. (Narrated by Ahmad"," Abu Dawood and Nasa’i and declared authentic by Ibn Hibban"," Darqutni and Hakim)."""
"224","It was narrated from Hazrat Abu Qatadah that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to lead us in prayer, and in the first two rak'ahs of Zuhr and Asr, he would recite Surah Al-Fatihah and two surahs, and sometimes he would recite a verse to us. He used to make the first rak'at long and in the last two rak'ats only read Fatiha-ul-Kitab. (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"225","Hazrat Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) narrates that we used to estimate the stay of the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) in the Zuhr and Asr prayers, so we estimated that he would stay in the first two rak'ats of Zuhr as long as he could recite Surah Al-Umm al-Sajdah, and in the last two rak'ats equal to half of the first two. And in the first two rak'ats of Asr, equal to the last two rak'ats of Zuhr, and in the last two rak'ats of Asr, half of the first two rak'ats of Asr. (Narrated by Muslim.)"
"226","Hazrat Sulaiman bin Yasar, may God have mercy on him, stated that so and so says that he lengthens the first two rak'ats of Zuhr, shortens the Asr prayer, recites Qasar Mufasal (short surahs) in the Maghrib prayer, recites the middle Mufasal in Isha and the full Mufasal in the morning prayer. So Hazrat Abu Huraira (RA) said: I have not offered a prayer similar to the prayer of the Prophet (PBUH) during the Imamate of anyone. (Narrated by Nasa'i with a valid chain of transmission.)"
"227","Hadhrat Jubayr Bin Mu'taam Radiyallahu Anhu narrates that I heard the Messenger of Allah (Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam) reciting a surah in Maghrib prayer. (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"228","Hazrat Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) used to recite Al-Umm Tanzeel (Sura Sajdah) in the first rak'ah of the Fajr prayer on Friday, and in the second rak'ah, Hal-i-Ali-ul-Insan (Surah Dahr). (Bukhari and Muslim) and it is narrated in Tabarani on the authority of Hazrat Ibn Mas'ud (RA) that he used to do this all the time."
"229","Hazrat Hudhayfah (RA) narrates that I prayed with the Prophet (PBUH), when a verse that mentioned the mercy of Allah would pass, he would stop there and ask for mercy, and when a verse of punishment would pass, he would stop there and ask for refuge from him. (It has been narrated by all five and Tirmidhi has described it as Hasan.)"
"230","Narrated by Hazrat Ibn Abbas, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \(People!) Listen"," I have been forbidden to recite the Qur'an while bowing and prostrating. So"," while bowing"," describe the greatness of your Lord and make supplications abundantly in prostration. This is worthy of your supplication being accepted.\"" (Narrated by Muslim)"""
"231","Hazrat Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, narrated that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, bowed and prostrated. Aghafirli] \So pure"," O Allah! O our Lord! With his praise. O Allah! Forgive me.'' used to read. (Bukhari and Muslim)"""
"232","It was narrated from Hazrat Abu Hurairah that when the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, intended to pray, he would say Allahu Akbar while standing up. Then when he went to bow, he would say Allahu Akbar at that time. Then when he raised his back from bowing, he would say [Sami'Allah limman hamidahu] and then when he stood straight from bowing, he would say [Rabbi wa lak al-hamdu]. Then he bowed for prostration while saying Takbeer. Then he would say Allahu Akbar while raising his head from prostration. Then while going into prostration, he would say Allahu Akbar, then while rising from prostration, he would say Allahu Akbar. Then he used to do the same in the whole prayer. Then when he got up after the second rak'at (reciting Tashahhud), he would say Allahu Akbar. (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"233","It was narrated from Hazrat Abu Saeed Khudri (RA) that when the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) would raise his head from bowing, O Allah! Rabbanna used to say... O Allah! O our Lord! Praise is only for You, so much praise that fills the heavens and the earth, and then everything that You want. O owner of praise and greatness! The best thing that a servant said... (Among the sayings of the servant, the saying \Rabbana Lak Al-Hamdu\"" has the most privilege to be said.) And we are all Your servants... O Allah! Whatever You give"," there is no one who can stop it"," and whatever You do not give"," there is no one who gives it"," and no one who has good luck and fortune can benefit from his greatness and fortune compared to Your punishment.” (Narrated by Muslim)."""
"234","On the authority of Hazrat Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \I have been ordered to prostrate on seven bones (parts): on the forehead... and pointed to my nose with my blessed hand... and with both hands on both knees and the edges of both feet.\"" (Bukhari and Muslim)"""
"235","It was narrated from Hazrat Ibn Bahina, may Allah be pleased with him, that when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed and prostrated, he would keep his arms apart from his sides until the whiteness of his armpits was visible. (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"236","On the authority of Hazrat Bara bin Azib, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \When you prostrate"," place your palms (on the ground) and raise your elbows.\"" (Narrated by Muslim.)"""
"237","It was narrated from Hazrat Wail bin Hajar (may Allah be pleased with him) that when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in Ruku, he would keep his fingers (of his hands) open, and when he was in Sajdah, he would keep his fingers (of his hands) together. (It has been narrated by Hakim)."
"238","Hazrat Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying while sitting on his four knees. (Narrated by Nasa'i and authenticated by Ibn Khuzima)."
"239","It was narrated from Hazrat Ibn Abbas (RA) that the Prophet (PBUH) used to recite this supplication between two prostrations: “O Allah! Forgive me, have mercy on me, guide me to the right path, grant me prosperity and grant me sustenance (halal). (This has been narrated by all four except Nasa'i. These words are Abu Dawud's, and Hakim has declared it as Sahih.)"
"240","Hazrat Malik bin Hawairat (RA) narrated that he saw the Prophet (PBUH) performing the Salat. (Narrated by Bukhari.)"
"241","It was narrated from Anas bin Malik (RA) that the Prophet (PBUH) recited the Qunut prayer after a full month of Ruku. In it, he cursed some of the tribes of the Arabs, then left it. (Bukhari and Muslim) Ahmad and Darqutni have narrated it in another way in the same way. There is so much increase in it that in the morning prayer, the Qunut prayers continue to live."
"242","It was narrated on the authority of Hazrat Anas that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite Qunut (otherwise he would not recite it) only when he prayed for a nation or cursed someone. (It has been declared Sahih by Ibn Khuzima)."
"243","Hazrat Saad bin Tariq Ashjaji (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated that I asked my father: Father! He prayed behind the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, Abu Bakr, Umar, Uthman and Ali. Did they all read Qunut in Fajr prayer? He replied that son! This is new. (Narrated by all five except Abu Dawood.)"
"244","Hazrat Hasan bin Ali (RA) narrated that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) taught me a few words so that I could recite them in the Qunut of Witr. (And they are:) [Allahhum! Oh Allah! Give me guidance and include me among those whom You have blessed with wisdom and guidance. And make me one of those whom You have blessed. And make me your friend by including me among those whom you have declared as your friend. Bless me in what You have given me and protect and save me from the evil of what You have decreed. Verily, the decision is issued only and the decision cannot be issued against you. And the one whom you have become a guardian can never be humiliated and disgraced. O our Lord! You are blessed and exalted.” (Narrated by all five.) Tabarani and Bayhaqi have also quoted the addition of [Wala Ya’iz mun Aadit]. That is, and from whom you cannot gain the honor of enmity. Also, in a different way, Nasa'i has also narrated the addition of [Wasal Allahu ali al-nabbii] at the end of this prayer. (There is a weakness in his document.)"
"245","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Huraira, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \When one of you prostrates"," he should not sit like a camel"," and he should place his hands on the ground before his knees.\"" (It has been narrated by all four of them. The witness of the first hadith is the hadith of Hazrat Ibn Umar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," which Ibn Khuzimah has declared authentic"," and Bukhari has described it as suspended.)"""
"246","It was narrated from Hazrat Ibn Umar that when the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, would sit for tashahhud, he would place his left hand on his left knee and his right hand on his right knee, and would tie the knot of fifty-three (53) and point with his index finger. (Narrated by Muslim.) And there is a tradition of Muslim that you would close all your fingers and point with the finger joined to the thumb."
"247","It was narrated on the authority of Hazrat Abdullah bin Masoud that the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, turned to us and said: “When one of you prays, he should say in tashahhud: [Al-Tahiyat-ul-Lillah … Alkh] “All verbal and financial worship is only for Allah.” O Prophet! Peace be upon you and may Allah's mercy and blessings be upon you. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is none worthy of worship except Allah, and I also bear witness that Hazrat Muhammad (peace be upon him) is the servant of Allah and His Messenger.\ Then he should choose the dua that he likes best and pray it.\"" (Bukhari and Muslim - Words are Bukhari's). And it is in the Musnad of Ahmad that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught him tashahhud and ordered him to teach it to the people. And it is narrated in Muslim on the authority of Hazrat Ibn Abbas"," may Allah be pleased with him"," that the Messenger of Allah"," may God bless him and grant him peace"," used to teach us tashahhud like this:"""
"248","It was narrated from Hazrat Fazla bin Ubayd (RA) that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) heard a man supplicating in his prayer. He did not praise Allah nor send blessings on the Prophet. He said: \He hastened.\"" Then he called him to him and said: \""When one of you begins to pray"," he should first recite the praises of his Lord"," then send blessings on the Prophet"," then pray for whatever he wants.\"""""
"249","Hazrat Abu Mas'ud Ansari (RA) narrates that Bashir bin Sa'd (RA) said: O Messenger of Allah! Allah Ta'ala has ordered us to send blessings on you, so how can we send blessings on you? You remained silent (for a while) then he said: Say thus: [Allahhum! Peace and blessings of Allah be upon him... Have mercy on Muhammad and the progeny of Muhammad, as You had mercy on Ibrahim (peace be upon him). And bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad as You blessed Abraham (peace be upon him) in the worlds. Indeed, He is of great attributes and is exalted.'' And peace be upon him, so he is as you know.''"
"250","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Hurairah, the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said: \When one of you has recited tashahhud"," he should seek refuge in Allah from four things and say: O Allah! I seek your refuge from the torment of hell"," from the torment of the grave"," from the temptation of death and life"," and from the evil of the temptation of Christ the Dajjal.\"" (Bukhari and Muslim) And there are also these words of a tradition in Muslim: \""When one of you is finished with the final tashahhud (then he should seek refuge with Allah from these four things).\"""""
"251","It was narrated from Hazrat Abu Bakr Siddique (RA) that I asked the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) to teach me such a supplication that I should recite in my prayers. He said: \Recite this: [Allahum! Ini zalamtu nafsi...etc. I have wronged my soul very much and there is no one who forgives sins except You"," so forgive me from Your Lordship and have mercy on me. Indeed"," He is the Most Forgiving and the Most Merciful.” (Bukhari and Muslim)"""
"252","Hazrat Wail bin Hajar (RA) narrates that I prayed with the Prophet (PBUH). Allah wa Barakatuh] used to say. (It was narrated by Abu Dawud with a valid chain of transmission.)"
"253","It was narrated from Hazrat Mughira bin Shuba that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite this dua at the end of every obligatory prayer: “There is no god but Allah.” And He has power over all things. O Allah! Whatever he gives, no one can stop him, and whatever he withholds, there is no one to give him. And no greatness can benefit someone who has respect and dignity in your presence.\ (Bukhari and Muslim)."""
"254","Hazrat Saad bin Abi Waqqas (RA) narrated that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) used to recite this tawzu at the end of every prayer (or after the prayer): [Allahum! Ini A'Uzubik Min Al-Bukhl...etc] \O Allah! I seek refuge in You from miserliness"," and I seek refuge in You from cowardice"," and I seek refuge in You from being returned to the worst age (very old age)"," and I seek refuge in You from the temptations of the world and the punishment of the grave.” (Narrated by Bukhari)"""
"255","It was narrated from Hazrat Thawban (RA) that when the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) returned the salutation, he would say [Astagfir-Allah] three times and then recite it. [God! O Allah! I seek your forgiveness. O Allah! So salam hai' means you are the one who is safe. And security is from You. O owner of greatness and honor! So he is blessed.” (Narrated by Muslim.)"
"256","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Hurairah, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Whoever recites [Subhan Allah] 33 times"," [Al-Hamdu Lillah] 33 times"," and [Allah Akbar] 33 times after saying the salutation of each prayer"," this is a total of 99\"" i.e. one less sleep"," and to complete the hundred [La \""There is no one but Allah"," and there is no partner.\"" He said"," \""All his sins are forgiven"," even if they are equal to the foam of the sea.\"" (It was narrated by Muslim.) And in another tradition"," he said: Allahu Akbar 34 times."""
"257","On the authority of Hazrat Mu'adh bin Jabal, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me: \O Mu'adh! I bequeath you never to forget these words after the end of every prayer [Allahum! ``O Allah! Give me Your remembrance"," Your gratitude"," and the ability to worship You best.”"""
"258","Hazrat Abu Umamah Radiyallahu Anhu narrates. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \Whoever recites Ayat al-Kursi after performing every obligatory prayer"," nothing can prevent him from entering Paradise except death.\"" (Also read Allah Ahad)."""
"259","On the authority of Hazrat Malik bin Huwayrth, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Pray the prayer in the same way as you have seen me pray.\"" (Narrated by Bukhari)."""
"260","Hazrat Imran bin Hussain (RA) narrates, 'The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said to me: \Pray while standing.\"" If you cannot pray standing"," then pray while sitting. And if you are unable to read while sitting"," read lying on your side. If you are unable to follow any of them"," then read it only with the hint.\"" (Narrated by Bukhari)."""
"261","It was narrated from Hazrat Jabir (RA) that the Prophet (PBUH) threw away the pillow of a patient who had prayed on a pillow and said: \If you have the strength"," pray on the ground; otherwise"," pray with your hands and lower your prostration slightly from Ruku.\"""""
"262","It was narrated from Abdullah Ibn Bahina, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led them to the Dhuhr prayer, and after performing two rak'ahs, he did not sit in tashahhud and stood up straight, and the people (muqtadi) also stood with him, even when he had finished the prayer and the people were waiting for him to return the salam. (It was narrated by all seven. And these words are from Bukhari.) And it is in the tradition of Muslim that he used to say Allahu Akbar while sitting for every prostration and people also prostrated with him (in tashahhud) in return for forgetting to sit. (He forgot to sit in tashahhud after two rak'ats, so he performed two prostrations to make up for it.)"
"263","Hazrat Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed two rakats in one of the two prayers of the previous evening (Zhuhr and Asr) and returned the salam. Hazrat Abu Bakr and Hazrat Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) were also present in the people (praying), both of them were afraid to talk to you (about it). And as soon as the people left the mosque, the people started asking (whispering to each other) whether the prayer has been shortened. There was a man whom the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called Dhuwalidin (because of his long hands). He said: O Messenger of Allah! Have you forgotten (today) or has the prayer been shortened? He said: \Neither have I forgotten nor have I reduced my prayer.\"" The person then said: Why not? Rather"," you have surely forgotten. Then he recited the two rak'ahs (which were missed) and performed the salutation"," then said Allahu Akbar and prostrated like his (usual) prostrations or longer than them. Then"," saying Allahu Akbar"," he raised his head. Then"," saying Allahu Akbar"," he placed the head on the ground and prostrated like his (usual) Sajdah"," or slightly longer than that"," and then raised his head saying Allahu Akbar. (Bukhari and Muslim - these words are Bukhari's. ) and there is a hadith of Muslim that it was the Asr prayer. And it is in the tradition of Abu Dawood that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) inquired: \""Did Dhuwalidin say the right thing?\"" So the people nodded their heads and said with gestures: \""Yes.\"" This addition is also in Sahihin"," but in them it is added with the word [Faqaluwa]. (He said with tongue. ) and it is in a tradition of Abu Dawud that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not prostrate until he was convinced by Allah. (Which is really weak. )."""
"264","It was narrated from Hazrat Imran bin Hussain (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught him the prayer, but he forgot it, so he made two prostrations, then recited the tashahhud, and then returned the salam. (It has been narrated by Abu Dawud and Tirmidhi and Tirmidhi has declared it good and Hakim has also narrated it and declared it Sahih.)"
"265","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \When one of you is in doubt about the prayer and does not know how many rak'ahs he has prayed"," three or four?\"" So"," in such a case"," leave the doubt and pray on the one you believe in. So if he has prayed five rak'ahs"," then these two prostrations will make his prayer double (being a substitute for one rak'ah"," making his prayer six rak'ahs) and if he has already prayed the whole prayer"," then these two prostrations will be a source of humiliation and humiliation for Satan (rubbing his nose).\"" (Narrated by Muslim)"""
"266","On the authority of Hazrat Abdullah bin Masoud, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah led the prayer. When he returned the greeting, it was said to him: O Messenger of Allah! Has anything new happened in prayer? He said: \What is that?\"" He said: You have performed so many prayers. It is narrated by Hazrat Ibn Masoud (RA) that he bowed both his feet and faced the Qibla and made two prostrations. Then he turned towards us and said: \""If something new had arisen in the prayer"," I would have informed you about it myself"," but I am also a human being like you.\"" And when one of you is in doubt about the prayer"," he should try to remember the correct situation"," then complete his prayer on that basis and then perform two prostrations.\"" (Bukhari and Muslim) And in another tradition of Bukhari: (He said: \""First) complete the prayer"," then return the salam and then prostrate.\"" And it is in the tradition of Muslim that the Prophet"," peace and blessings be upon him"," performed the prostration after the Sahu Salam wa Kalam. Musnad Ahmad"," Abu Dawud and There is a hadith in Nasa'i on the authority of Hazrat Abdullah bin Jafar"," may Allah be pleased with him: \""A person who is in doubt about the prayer"," should perform two prostrations after returning the salam.\"""""
"267","It was narrated on the authority of Hazrat Mughira bin Shuba, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \When one of you is in doubt"," and he stands up after two rak'ats"," even if he stands up straight"," then he should continue with the next rak'at and not turn back"," and then perform two prostrations of Suhu.\"" And if he is not standing straight"," he should sit. And in this case it is not permissible to prostrate on it."""
"268","It is narrated from Hazrat Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \There is no prostration to a muqtadi.\"" Yes"," if the imam forgets"," then the prostration is suho on both the imam and the muqtadi."""
"269","Narrated by Hazrat Thawban, may Allah be pleased with him: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \There are two prostrations for every sahu"," which is after the return of salam.\"""""
"270","It was narrated from Hazrat Abu Huraira (RA) that we recited Sajdah with the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) in Surah (Iza-as-Samai Anshaqat) and Surah (Read in the Name of the Lord). (Narrated by Muslim.)"
"271","It was narrated from Hazrat Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Sajdah of Surah Sa is not one of those that have been mentioned with emphasis and emphasis. (Narrated by Bukhari.)"
"272","It was narrated from Hazrat Ibn Abbas (RA) that the Prophet (PBUH) recited Sajdah in Surah Najm. (Narrated by Bukhari.)"
"273","It was narrated from Hazrat Zayd bin Thabit (RA) that I recited Surah Najam in front of the Prophet (PBUH), but he did not recite Sajdah in it. (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"274","It was narrated from Hazrat Khalid bin Madan, may God have mercy on him, that Surah Hajj has been given excellence because of its two prostrations. (It was mentioned by Abu Dawood in Murasil.) And it was narrated by Ahmad and Tirmidhi from Hazrat Uqbah bin Amir (RA) and there is this addition: “Whoever does not want to perform these two prostrations, should not recite this (Surat).” (Its chain of transmission is weak.)"
"275","On the authority of Hazrat Umar, he said: People! We pass by the prostrations (of the recitation) (reciting their verses). (Narrated by Al-Bukhari.) And in Muta, there are these words: Allah Almighty has not made prostration obligatory, but we should prostrate if we wish."
"276","It was narrated from Hazrat Ibn Umar that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite the Qur'an in front of us. (Narrated by Abu Dawud with weak chain of transmission.)"
"277","It was narrated from Hazrat Abu Bakra (RA) that whenever the Prophet (PBUH) received any good news, he would prostrate before Allah. (Narrated by all five except Nasa'i)."
"278","It was narrated on the authority of Hazrat Abd al-Rahman bin Awf (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrated and prostrated for a long time."
"279","It was narrated from Bara bin Azib that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Hazrat Ali to Yemen. The narrator narrated the hadith in which he said that Hazrat Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) sent the invitation to the people of Yemen to accept Islam. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) read that letter, he prostrated to thank Allah for it. (Narrated by Bayhaqi and original in Bukhari.)"
"280","Hazrat Rabi'ah bin Ka'b Aslami (RA) narrates that one day the Prophet (SAW) said to me: \Ask (whatever you have to ask).\"" I said: \""I seek your companionship in Paradise.\"" He said: \""Is there anything else?\"" I said: That is all that is required. He said: \""Then help me by prostrating a lot to achieve your meaning.\"" (Narrated by Muslim)."""
"281","On the authority of Hazrat Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I remember ten rak'ahs of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): two rak'ahs before the Zuhr prayer and two after it. And after Maghrib, two rakats at home. Two rakats of Isha at home after the obligatory prayer. And two rak'ahs before dawn. In a tradition of both (Bukhari and Muslim) and (Bukhari and Muslim) it is also said that two rak'ahs were (read) at home after the Friday prayer. And in the tradition of Muslim it is also said that he used to pray only two light rak'ahs after the morning prayer."
"282","It was narrated from Hazrat Aisha that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not miss four rak'ahs before the Zuhr prayer and two rak'ahs before the Fajr prayer. (Narrated by Bukhari.)"
"283","It is narrated from Hazrat Aisha that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to arrange the two sunnahs of Fajr the most. (Bukhari and Muslim) and Muslim says that the two rakats (sunnahs) of the Fajr prayer are better than the world and Mafiha."
"284","Umm al-Mu'minin Hazrat Umm Habiba (RA) narrated that I heard the Messenger of Allah (SAW) saying: \Whoever recites twelve rak'ahs of Nawafil day and night"," a house will be built in Paradise for him.\"" And it is the same in the hadith of Tirmidhi"," and it is more clear in it: \""Four rak'ats before Zuhr and two rak'ats after it"," and two rak'ats after the Maghrib prayer"," and two rak'ats after the 'Isha' prayer and two rak'ats before the Fajr prayer.\"" It does."""
"285","On the authority of Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \May Allah have mercy on the person who prays four rak'ahs before Asr prayer.\"""""
"286","Hazrat Abdullah bin Mughfil Muzni (RA) narrated from the Prophet (PBUH) that he said: “Pray before Maghrib. (Narrated by Al-Bukhari.) In a tradition of Ibn Hibban, it is said that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed two rak'ahs before Maghrib. And in Muslim it is narrated from Hazrat Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that we used to pray two rak'ahs after sunset (before the obligatory prayer) and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was looking at us."
"287","Hazrat Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite two rak'ahs before the Fajr prayer so lightly that I wondered if he had recited Umm al-Kitab (Fatihah) as well (or not). (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"288","It was narrated from Hazrat Abu Huraira that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited (in the first of the two rak'ahs of Fajr) (Qul-ya-iha-ul-kafiroon) (and (in the second)) (say) (Qul-hu-Allah-hu-ahadmo). (Narrated by Muslim.)"
"289","It was narrated from Hazrat Aisha that when the Prophet (peace be upon him) finished reciting the two sunnahs of the Fajr prayer, he would lie down on his right side. (Narrated by Bukhari.)"
"290","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \When one of you has prayed two rak'ahs before the Fajr prayer"," he should lie down on his right side.\"""""
"291","On the authority of Hazrat Abdullah bin Umar, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \The night prayer consists of two rak'ahs"," and when one of you fears the dawn"," he should pray one rak'ah (at the end). This first rak'at will make his entire prayer a witr (odd).\"" (Bukhari and Muslim) and the words of the traditions of all five are as follows: \""The day and night prayers are two rak'ats.\"""""
"292","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Hurairah, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \The best prayer after the obligatory prayer is the night prayer.\"" (Narrated by Muslim)."""
"293","Narrated by Hazrat Abu Ayyub Ansari, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Witr is a right for every Muslim (it must be performed). Whoever likes to recite five Witrs should do so"," and whoever likes to recite three Witrs should do so"," and whoever likes to recite one Witr should do so.\"" .)"""
"294","Hazrat Ali bin Abi Talib (RA) narrated that Witr is not final and mandatory like Fards, but it is a Sunnah that was prescribed by the Messenger of Allah (PBUH). (Nisa'i and Tirmidhi have described it, and Tirmidhi has called it good, and Hakim has narrated it and said it is correct.)"
"295","On the authority of Hazrat Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, stayed in the month of Ramadan, then the next night the Companions waited for him and he did not come out (of the room). He said: \I had this desire that this Witr prayer should not be made obligatory on you.\"" (Narrated by Ibn Hibban)."""
"296","On the authority of Hazrat Al-Khaza bin Hudhafa, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Allah has helped you with a prayer that is better for you than red camels.\"" We said: O Messenger of Allah! Which prayer is that? He said: \""The prayer of Witr"," which is between the Isha prayer and the dawn prayer.\"" (It has been narrated by five people except Nasa'i"," and Hakim has declared it authentic.) Ahmad has narrated a tradition similar to it from Amr bin Shuaib"," from his father"," and from his grandfather."""
"297","Hazrat Abdullah, may God have mercy on him, narrates from his father, Hazrat Burida, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Witr is right.\"" He who does not recite Witr has nothing to do with us.” (It was narrated by Abu Dawud with a weak chain of transmission and Al-Hakim said it to be Sahih. There is also a witness of this in the Musnad of Ahmad which was narrated by Hazrat Abu Hurairah"," but it is weak.)"""
"298","It was narrated from Hazrat Aisha that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not pray more than eleven rak'ahs in Ramadan and non-Ramadan. (Earlier) he used to perform four rak'ahs in such a way that do not ask about their beauty and their length. Then he used to pray three rakats. Hazrat Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated that I said: O Messenger of Allah! Do you go to sleep before performing Witr? He said: \Aisha! My two eyes sleep"," my heart does not sleep.'' And after that they would read two rakats of Fajr. Thirteen rak'ahs were performed (all together)."""
"299","It was narrated from Hazrat Aisha that the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, used to perform thirteen rak'ahs at night. They used to have five Witrs and in these five Witrs, they used to sit only in the last rakat for Tashahhud."
"300","It was narrated from Hazrat Aisha that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to recite Witr in every part of the night, and his Witr reading even reached dawn. (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"301","It was narrated on the authority of Hazrat Abdullah bin Amr bin As, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me: “O Abdullah! Don't become like so-and-so man. He used to stay in Al-Lil, then later he abandoned it.\ (Bukhari and Muslim)."""
"302","On the authority of Hazrat Ali bin Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O people of the Qur’an! Read Witr. Allah himself is witr (one) and loves witr.”"
"303","On the authority of Hazrat Ibn Umar, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Make Witr the last prayer of your night.\"" (Bukhari and Muslim)"""
"304","It was narrated from Hazrat Talaq bin Ali (RA) that I heard the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) say: “No witr twice in one night.”"
"305","It was narrated from Hazrat Abi bin Ka'b (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah, may God's prayers and peace be upon him, used to recite (three rak'ats) in witr respectively: (Glory be to the name of the Most High) and (Qulhu Allahu Ahad) respectively. (It was narrated by Ahmad, Abu Dawud and Nasa'i.) And Nasa'i also narrated this addition: Salaam used to be performed in the last rak'ah only. Abu Dawud and Tirmidhi have narrated in the same way from Hazrat Aisha and it is in this hadith that he used to recite one surah in each rak'at and in the last rak'at he used to recite (Qul huwa Allahu ahad) and Mu'awaddin."
"306","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Recite Witr before dawn.\"" (Narrated by Muslim.) And in Ibn Hibban: \""Whoever wakes up in the morning and does not recite Witr"," then he has no Witr.\"""""
"307","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Whoever falls asleep after reciting Witr (eyes not open) or does not remember it"," then he should recite it in the morning or when he remembers it.\"""""
"308","On the authority of Hazrat Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Whoever fears that he will not be able to wake up in the last part of the night"," then he should recite Witr in the first part of the night.\"" And whoever has the expectation and hope that he will wake up"," then he should recite Witr in the last part of the night"," because the angels are present in the prayer in the last part of the night"," and this is much better.\"" (Muslim tradition has done this)."""
"309","On the authority of Hazrat Abdullah bin Umar, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \When Fajr dawns"," then the time for every prayer and witr that was recited at night ends (ends)"," so you should recite the witr first before dawn.\"" (Narrated by Tirmidhi)."""
"310","It was narrated from Hazrat Aisha that the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, used to pray four rak'ats of Zuha prayer and would pray more as much as Allah willed. (Narrated by Muslim.) And in Muslim it is narrated from Hazrat Aisha that she was asked: Did the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, lead the Zuha prayer? So he said no, except when he comes back from a trip. And it is narrated in Muslim only on the authority of Hazrat Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that I never saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performing the Zuha prayer while I was performing this Nawafil."
"311","On the authority of Hazrat Zaid bin Arqam, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \The time for the Awabeen (those who turn to Allah) to pray is when the young camels start to feel burning due to the heat.\"" (Narrated by Tirmidhi)."""
"312","It was narrated from Hazrat Anas that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Whoever recites twelve rak'ahs of the Zuha prayer"," Allah will build for him a palace in Paradise.\"""""
"313","It was narrated from Hazrat Aisha that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to my house and offered eight rak'ahs of the Zuha prayer. (It was narrated by Ibn Hibban in his Sahih)."
"314","On the authority of Hazrat Abdullah bin Umar, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Praying in congregation is twenty-seven degrees more excellent than the prayer of a single person.\"" (Bukhari and Muslim) And in Bukhari and Muslim"," it is narrated on the authority of Hazrat Abu Huraira"," may Allah be pleased with him: \""The reward is twenty-five degrees higher.\"" And in the same way"," it is narrated in Bukhari from Hazrat Abu Saeed Al-Khudri"," may Allah be pleased with him"," but there is only one place in it. is the word of"""
"315","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Huraira, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “By the One in Whose Hand is my soul! I intended that I should order the wood, so that it should be collected, then order the prayer, and the call to prayer should be called for it, then order a man to lead the people, then I myself would go after those people who do not join in the prayer, then (if they were present in their houses) I would set their houses on fire and burn them. Oath of the beloved in whose hands is my life! If one of them comes to know that he will find a thick bone full of meat or two beautiful feet, then he must attend the Isha prayer."
"316","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Huraira, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \The most burdensome and burdensome on the hypocrites are the Isha prayer and the Fajr prayer"," and if they know the (great reward) that is in both of them"," then they must join them"," even if they have to come on their knees.\"" (Bukhari and Muslim)"""
"317","It was narrated on the authority of Hazrat Abu Huraira that a blind man came to the service of the Prophet (peace be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah! I don't have a man to catch me and bring me to the mosque. He gave him leave (so that he should pray at home). So when he started to return, he called him and asked: \Do you hear the call to prayer?\"" He said: \""Yes.\"""""
"318","On the authority of Hazrat Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever hears the call to prayer, then does not join the congregational prayer, there is no prayer for him, except that there is an excuse.” (Narrated by Ibn Majah, Darqutni, Ibn Hibban and Al-Hakim, and its chain of transmission is in accordance with the condition of Muslim, but some have preferred that it be suspended.)"
"319","It was narrated from Hazrat Yazid bin Aswad (RA) that he prayed the morning prayer with the Messenger of Allah (PBUH). When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had prayed, he saw two men who had not prayed (with him). You called them both to you. When they were brought to your service, their shoulders were trembling (from fear). He inquired: \What prevented you from praying with us?\"" He said: We had prayed in our homes. He said: \""Don't do that.\"" If you pray in your homes"," then you find the imam who has not yet prayed"," then pray with him"," and it will become nafl for you.”"""
"320","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \The Imam is appointed so that he is followed.\"" So when he says Allahu Akbar"," you also say Allahu Akbar"," and you do not say Allahu Akbar"," even if the Imam says Allahu Akbar. And when he bows"," you also bow. And do not bow until the Imam bows. And when the Imam says"," ``Sami'-Allah liman Hamidahu"," then you Allah! Say"," Lord"," praise be to you. And when he prostrates"," you also prostrate. Do not prostrate even when the Imam prostrates. And when the Imam prays standing"," you also pray standing"," and when he prays sitting"," all of you pray sitting.\"""""
"321","It was narrated from Hazrat Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) saw his Companions retreating, so he said: \Come forward and follow me"," and let those behind you follow you.\"" (Narrated by Muslim)"""
"322","Hazrat Zayd bin Thabit (RA) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) made a small (tent-like) room out of a mat and started praying in it. People also inquired and found out and they came and joined you in prayer. This is a long hadith. And there is also in it that (he said:) \Apart from the obligatory prayer"," the best prayer for a man is that which he performs at home.\"" (Bukhari and Muslim)."""
"323","It was narrated from Hazrat Jabir (RA) that Hazrat Mu'adh (RA) led his followers in the Isha prayer. He prolonged the reading, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \O Mu'adh! Does he want to make the worshipers fall into temptation? When you lead the people"," then recite (Wal-Shams and Wa-Duhaha) 'Glory be to the Name of the Most High'"," 'Recite in the Name of the Lord' and 'Wal-Layl Idha-Yaghshi' (Bukhari and Muslim). (The words are Muslim.)"""
"324","Hazrat Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, says, in the context of the prayer of the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, which he taught to people in the state of illness: He came and sat on the left side of Hazrat Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him. So you were teaching the people sitting and praying while Hazrat Abu Bakr (RA) was standing. Hazrat Abu Bakr (RA) was following the example of the Prophet (PBUH) and people were praying following Hazrat Abu Bakr (RA). (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"325","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \When one of you leads the people"," he should reduce his recitation"," because among the muqtadas there are children"," old people"," weak and needy people.\"" Yes"," when he prays alone"," he should pray in any way he wants.” (Bukhari and Muslim)"""
"326","It was narrated from Hazrat Amr bin Salama that my father said to his people: I am coming to you from the true Prophet. He said: \When it is time for prayer"," one of you should say the call to prayer"," and let a person who recites the Holy Qur'an the most (hafiz) lead.\"" I was six or seven years old at that time. (Narrated by Bukhari"," Abu Dawud and Nasa'i.)"""
"327","It is narrated from Hazrat Ibn Masoud, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \The Imam of the people should be a man who recites the Holy Qur'an a lot","\"" that is"," a Hafiz. If people are equal in this attribute"," then he who has more knowledge of the Prophet's Sunnah becomes the imam. And if the people are equal in the knowledge of the Sunnah"," then the one who migrated first becomes the imam. If all are equal in this attribute"," then he who has accepted Islam first becomes Imam. And in one hadith there is also the word Sinna (age) instead of Silma (Islam)."""
"328","In Sunan Ibn Majah, it is narrated from Hazrat Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, that \No woman should become the imam of a man"," nor should a Bedouin lead a migrant"," nor should a fajr become the imam of a believer.\"" (The authenticity of this hadith is weak.)"""
"329","Narrated by Hazrat Anas, the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \Keep your ranks firmly together and do not leave a gap between them"," and keep your necks level with each other.\"""""
"330","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Hurairah, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \The best (most virtuous) ranks of men are the first among them"," and the bad (lowest) ranks are the last among them.\"" And the best row of women is the last among them and the worst row is the first among them. (Narrated by Muslim.)"""
"331","On the authority of Hazrat Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said that I prayed with the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, one night. I stood on your left side, so the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, held my head from behind and made me stand on his right side. (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"332","It was narrated from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that when the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him) led the prayer, I and an orphan (boy) stood behind him and Umm Salim (may Allah be pleased with him) stood alone behind us. (Bukhari and Muslim - words are Bukhari's)."
"333","Hazrat Abu Bakra (may God be pleased with him) said that he reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) just when he was in the position of bowing, so he bowed before reaching the row, then (walking in the position of bowing) he reached the row. What is it that he bowed before joining the row, then walked in the same state and joined the row."
"334","It was narrated from Hazrat Wabsa bin Mabad, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw a man who was standing alone at the back of the row praying. You ordered him to return the prayer. (It was narrated by Ahmad, Abu Dawud and Tirmidhi. Tirmidhi said Hasan and Ibn Hibban are correct.) And in Ibn Hibban, there is a narration from Talaq bin Ali, may God be pleased with him: “A person does not pray alone behind the row.” And Tabarani has also quoted such an addition in the hadith of Wabsa: “Why didn’t you enter with them, or else you would have pulled back a person praying (from the first row).”"
"335","Hazrat Abu Huraira (RA) narrated from the Prophet (PBUH) that he said: \When you hear the Iqamah of the prayer"," walk towards the prayer with contentment"," calmness and dignity.\"" Do not speed up. Then pray as much as you can with the congregational prayer and complete what remains (later).” (Bukhari and Muslim – words are Bukhari’s)."""
"336","On the authority of Hazrat Abi bin Ka'b, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \A person praying together with another person is more pure and more rewarding than praying alone.\"" And praying together with two men is more rewarding than praying together with one man. In the same way"," the more people there are"," the more beloved they are to Allah.”"""
"337","Hazrat Umm Waraqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered her to lead her family."
"338","Anas (RA) narrated that the Prophet (PBUH) appointed Ibn Umm Maktoum (RA) as his deputy. He used to lead the people even though he was blind. (This hadith has been narrated by Ahmad and Abu Dawud and Ibn Hibban has also narrated a hadith of the same meaning from Hazrat Aisha (RA).)"
"339","On the authority of Hazrat Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever says [La ilaha illa Allah] with his tongue, offer his funeral prayer, and whoever says [La ilaha illa Allah], also offer the prayer behind him.”"
"340","On the authority of Hazrat Ali bin Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \When one of you comes to pray"," he should join the Imam in the state in which he finds him and do what the Imam does.\"""""
"341","Hazrat Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) stated that in the beginning, two rak'ahs (of traveling and visiting) were obligatory. (Bukhari and Muslim) and in a tradition of Bukhari, then the prayer of migration was made obligatory with four rakats and the prayer of travel was maintained in the first state. Ahmad has added so much that except for the Maghrib prayer because it is the Witr of the day and except for the morning prayer because the recitation is prolonged in this prayer."
"342","Hazrat Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would (sometimes) pray short and (sometimes) full prayers while traveling, and (also sometimes) fast and (sometimes) skip them. (It was narrated by Darqutni and its narrators are reliable, but the hadith is Maaloool. And it is safe that Hazrat Aisha used to do this herself.) And he said: It is not incumbent on me to do this. (Narrated by Bayhaqi)."
"343","Hazrat Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Allah, the Exalted, likes that in the deeds He has given leave to be followed, just as He dislikes the doing of sinful deeds.” Let's go."
"344","It was narrated from Hazrat Anas that the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, used to perform two rak'ahs (short prayer) when he traveled for a distance of three miles or three farsakhs. (Narrated by Muslim.)"
"345","Narrated by Hazrat Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: We traveled with the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, from Madinah to Makkah. (Bukhari and Muslim - words are Bukhari's)."
"346","Hazrat Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stayed for 19 days (during these days) and he continued to pay Qasr. And there is a tradition that he stayed in Makkah for 19 days. (It was narrated by Bukhari.) And in the tradition of Abu Dawud, 17 days are mentioned, and in another tradition, 15 days. And in Abu Dawood it is narrated from Hazrat Imran bin Hussain that his period of stay was 18 days. And in this, Hazrat Jabir Radiyallahu Anhu says that he stayed in Tabuk for twenty (20) days and continued to perform short prayers. The narrators of this hadith are reliable, but there is a difference in its reception."
"347","It was narrated from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) started his journey before sunset, he would postpone the Zuhr prayer until Asr time, then he would get down from his horse and perform both the Zuhr and Asr prayers together. And when the sun would set before the start of the journey, then after performing the Zuhr prayer, they would mount and leave for the journey. (Bukhari and Muslim) and it is from the authentic chain of command in Arbaeen that he offered the Zuhr and Asr prayers, then mounted the ride. And it is in Abu Na'im's \Mustakhir Muslim\"" that when he was on a journey and the sun was setting"," he would perform both Zuhr and Asr together and set out from there."""
"348","It was narrated from Hazrat Muadh bin Jabal, may Allah be pleased with him, that when we went out with the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, in the battle of Tabuk, he used to pray Zuhr and Asr prayers together. (Narrated by Muslim.)"
"349","On the authority of Hazrat Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Do not shorten the prayer to a distance of less than four burads. Four burads are the distance from Makkah to Isfan.\"""""
"350","On the authority of Hazrat Jabir, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \The best people of my ummah are those who ask for forgiveness when an evil is done to them"," and when they are on a journey"," they arrange short prayers and do not fast.\"""""
"351","It was narrated from Hazrat Imran bin Hussain (RA) that I was suffering from hemorrhoids. I asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about praying, and he said: \Pray standing. If you cannot pray standing"," then pray sitting.\"" And if you do not have the strength"," then pray lying on your side."""
"352","It was narrated from Hazrat Jabir that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited a sick person and saw that he was praying on a pillow. He threw that pillow away and said: \Pray on the ground\"" if you can"," otherwise pray with gestures. Yes"," bow a little more than bowing for your prostrations."""
"353","Hazrat Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) reported that I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying (on all fours). (Narrated by Nasa'i and confirmed by Al-Hakim as Sahih.)"
"354","It was narrated from Hazrat Abdullah bin Umar and Hazrat Abu Huraira that they heard the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, say on his pulpit: \People must refrain from skipping the Friday prayer"," otherwise Allah will seal their hearts"," then they will be among the heedless.\"" (Narrated by Muslim)"""
"355","It was narrated from Hazrat Salama bin Akua, may Allah be pleased with him, that we used to pray Friday with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. Then when we finished Friday and went to our homes, there was no shade of the walls at that time, so that we could sit and rest in it (or walk in its shade to reach home). (Bukhari and Muslim - the words are Bukhari)."
"356","It was narrated from Hazrat Sahl bin Saad, may Allah be pleased with him, that (on Fridays), we used to arrange Qailulah (afternoon rest) and food after Friday prayers. (Bukhari and Muslim - the words are from Muslim.) And there is a hadith: We used to do this during the blessed era of the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"357","Hazrat Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) reported that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was delivering the Friday sermon when a merchant caravan came from Syria. All the people hastened towards this caravan and only twelve men remained (to hear the sermon). (Narrated by Muslim.)"
"358","On the authority of Hazrat Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Whoever completes one rak'ah (in congregation) of the Friday prayer or any other prayer"," then he should join the second rak'ah (the rest of the prayer) with it.\"" And his prayer will be completed.” (Narrated by Nasa’i Ibn Majah and Darqutni. These words are from Darqutni and its chain of transmission is authentic"," but Abu Hatim has declared its transmission to be strong.)"""
"359","It was narrated from Hazrat Jabir bin Samrah (RA) that the Prophet (PBUH) used to deliver the Friday sermon while standing, then he would sit down (a little in the middle) and then he would speak standing up. (Narrated by Muslim.)"
"360","It was narrated from Hazrat Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would give a sermon, his eyes would turn red, his voice would become loud and his anger would become strong, even his condition would become as if he was threatening an army (of attack) that \the enemy's army will arrive in the morning or in the evening\"" and he would say: \""After praise and prayer\"" the best thing is the Book of Allah and the best way is the way of Muhammad (peace be upon him). The worst (of deeds) are new deeds and every innovation is misguidance. (Narrated by Muslim.) And it is in a tradition of Muslim: The sermon of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on Fridays used to be that he would recite the praises of Allah. And in a hadith of Muslim"," it is: \""Whoever Allah guides to the right path"," there is no one who can misguide him"," and whomever He leads astray"," there is no one who can guide him.\"""""
"361","On the authority of Hazrat Ammar bin Yasir, may Allah be pleased with him, that I heard the Messenger of Allah say: \The length of a man's prayer and the brevity of his sermon is a sign of his jurisprudence.\"" (Narrated by Muslim)."""
"362","Hazrat Umm Hisham bint Harithah (RA) narrates that I memorized Surah Qa from the words of the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) every Friday. (Narrated by Muslim.)"
"363","On the authority of Hazrat Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \The person who speaks on Friday when the Imam is delivering the sermon is like a donkey carrying books.\"" And the person who told him to be silent is not his Friday.” (Narrated by Ahmad in a chain of transmission in which there is no problem.) And this hadith interprets the hadith narrated by Hazrat Abu Hurairah"," may Allah be pleased with him"," which is authentically narrated in Sahihin: “When you said to your companion on Friday"," ‘Be quiet","’ while the Imam was delivering the sermon"," you also spoke nonsense.”"""
"364","It is narrated by Hazrat Jabir that a man entered the mosque on Friday. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was giving a sermon at that time. He asked him: \Have you prayed?\"" He said: No. He said: \""Get up and pray two rak'ahs.\"" (Bukhari and Muslim)."""
"365","It was narrated from Hazrat Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to recite Surah Juma and Surah Al-Munafiqun in the Friday prayer. (Narrated by Muslim.) And in a tradition of Muslim, it was narrated from Hazrat Numan bin Basheer (RA) that he (PBUH) used to recite (Sabhi Asma Rabbik Al-Ala) and (Hal Ataq Hadeeth Al Ghashiyyah) in the Eid prayers and Friday prayers."
"366","It was narrated from Hazrat Zaid bin Arqam that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) offered the Eid prayer and gave permission for Friday and said: \Whoever wants to read"," let him read.\"""""
"367","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Hurairah, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \When one of you prays on Friday"," he should pray four rak'ahs after that.\"" (Narrated by Muslim)."""
"368","Hazrat Saib bin Yazid (may Allah be pleased with him) reported that Hazrat Muawiya (may Allah be pleased with him) said: When you offer the Friday prayer, do not combine it with another prayer, even if you talk to someone or leave it, because the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered us not to combine any prayer with another prayer, even if we talk to someone or leave it. (Narrated by Muslim.)"
"369","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Hurairah, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Whoever takes a bath and comes for Friday"," then prays as much as is necessary for him"," then sits quietly until the Imam finishes the Friday sermon"," then performs the obligatory prayer with the Imam"," then his sins between the two Fridays are forgiven"," as well as for three more days.\"" (Narrated by Muslim)"""
"370","It was narrated from Hazrat Abu Huraira that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, mentioned the day of Friday and said: \There is an hour in it that if a Muslim asks Allah for something while praying at this hour"," Allah will surely grant him.\"" And he indicated with his blessed hand that that time is very short. (Bukhari and Muslim) And in a hadith of Muslim: That time is light."""
"371","Hazrat Abu Burda (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated from his father Hazrat (Abu Musa al-Ash’ari, may God be pleased with him) that his father said that I heard the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him) say: “That hour is from the time when the Imam sits on the pulpit until the end of the congregation.” (Narrated by Muslim.) And on the authority of Hazrat Abdullah ibn Salam (RA) on the authority of Ibn Majah and on the authority of Hazrat Jabir (RA) on the authority of Abu Dawud and Nasa’i: That hour is between the Asr prayer and sunset. There is a lot of disagreement about this clock, even there are more than forty sayings (opinions) about it. I have written all of them in (Fath al-Bari) Sharh Bukhari."
"372","On the authority of Hazrat Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: It has been the practice that there are forty or more Fridays. (It has been narrated by Darqutni with weak chain of transmission.)"
"373","It was narrated from Hazrat Samura bin Jundab (RA) that the Prophet (PBUH) used to pray for forgiveness for believing men and believing women every Friday. (Narrated by Bazar with a weak chain of transmission.)"
"374","It was narrated from Hazrat Jabir bin Samrah (RA) that the Prophet (PBUH) used to give advice to the people by reciting a few verses of the Holy Qur'an in the Friday sermon. (It was narrated by Abu Dawud and its original is in Muslim.)"
"375","On the authority of Hazrat Tariq bin Shihab, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \It is obligatory on every Muslim to pray Friday in congregation"," but four types of people are exempt from it: slaves"," women"," children"," and the sick.\"" (Narrated by Abu Dawood"," and (at the same time) it has also been said that Tariq"," may Allah be pleased with him"," did not hear (directly) from the Prophet"," may Allah bless him and grant him peace). has been done) has narrated on the authority of Hazrat Abu Musa (may God be pleased with him)."""
"376","On the authority of Hazrat Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Friday is not obligatory on a traveler.\"""""
"377","It was narrated from Hazrat Abdullah bin Masoud that when the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, would stand on the pulpit, we would turn our faces towards him. (It was narrated by Tirmidhi with a weak chain of transmission. One of its witnesses is from the hadith of Hazrat Bara in Ibn Khuzimah.)"
"378","It was narrated from Hazrat Haqm bin Huzn (RA) that we were present with the Prophet (PBUH) on Friday. You stood with the support of a stick or a bow. (It was narrated by Abu Dawud.)"
"379","Hazrat Saleh bin Khawat (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated from a person who prayed the prayer of fear with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Zaat al-Raqqa. This person narrated that a group of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) lined up with him for prayer and another group lined up in front of him to fight the enemy. You offered one rak'at to those who were standing in a row with you, then you stood straight and they completed the rest of the prayer on their own, then they left and went and lined up in front of the enemy and another group came. You offered him one of your remaining rak'ahs, then you remained seated and he completed the prayer on his own in the meantime, then you exchanged salutations with him. (Bukhari and Muslim - the words are from Muslim. In Ibn Mundah's (book) al-Marifah, Salih bin Khawat narrates this tradition from his father.)"
"380","It was narrated from Hazrat Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) that I went to Najd in the company of the Prophet (peace be upon him). When we found the enemy in front of us, we formed ranks opposite them. And the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up and led us in prayer. A group stood with you to pray and a group stood in front of the enemy. The group that was with you (participating in prayer) bowed with you one ruku and two prostrations and went back to the place of the group that had not yet prayed. Then the members of this group came, he also bowed with them and performed two prostrations, then he returned the salutation, but each of them (groups) stood up (paying their Rak'at separately) and performed one bow and two prostrations. (Bukhari and Muslim - words are Bukhari's)."
"381","It was narrated from Hazrat Jabir (RA) that I was present with the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) in fear of prayer. We made two arrays. A row stood behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while the enemy was between us and the Qibla. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said Allahu Akbar and we all said Allahu Akbar. Then he bowed and we all bowed. Then he raised his head from bowing and we all raised our heads. When you have completed the Sajdah, the row that was closest to you stood up. Then the narrator narrated the entire hadith. In another tradition, he then prostrated and the first row also prostrated with him, then when they all stood up, the second row went into prostration. And then the first row moved back and the second row moved forward. And (further hadith) narrated his simil. And at the end of it, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned the greeting and we all also returned the greeting. (Narrated by Muslim.) And Abu Dawud narrated a similar tradition from Abu Ayyash Zarqi (may Allah be pleased with him) but he added that it was (performed) at the place of Isfan. And there is a tradition in Nasa'i from Hazrat Jabir (R.A.) with another chain of transmission that the Prophet (S.A.W.) led a group of his Companions in two rak'ahs, then returned the salam. Then the other group recited two rak'ahs in the same way and greeted them. And there is a similar narration in Abu Dawood from Hazrat Abu Bakra (RA)."
"382","It was narrated from Hazrat Hudhayfah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) offered one rak'ah to those people and he also offered one rak'ah to them. And they did not complete the prayer. (It was narrated by Ahmad, Abu Dawud and Nasa’i and Ibn Hibban declared it to be Sahih. Ibn Khuzima narrated a similar hadith on the authority of Hazrat Ibn Abbas.)"
"383","Hazrat Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \The prayer of fear is one rak'ah no matter how it is performed.\"""""
"384","It was narrated on the authority of Hazrat Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him: \Najmaz is not prostration in fear.\"""""
"385","On the authority of Hazrat Aisha, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Eid-ul-Fitr is the day when people break their fast. And Eid al-Adha is the day on which people perform sacrifices.” (Narrated by Tirmidhi)."
"386","Hazrat Abu Umayr bin Anas (may Allah have mercy on him) narrates from his uncles who were companions of the Prophet (peace be upon him) that some horsemen came (to his service) and testified that we had seen the moon yesterday evening. He commanded: \Break the fast and come to your Eidgah tomorrow morning (for the Eid prayer).\"""""
"387","It was narrated from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not go out (for prayer) on the day of Eid al-Fitr until he had eaten a few dates in an odd number. (Narrated by Al-Bukhari.) And it is mentioned in a suspended tradition that Imam Ahmad received that he used to eat these dates one by one."
"388","Hadhrat (Abdullah) Ibn Burida, may God have mercy on him, narrates from his father (Burida, may God be pleased with him): He said that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, would not go out without eating something for the Eid al-Fitr prayer. (Narrated by Ahmad and Tirmidhi and declared authentic by Ibn Hibban.)"
"389","It was narrated from Hazrat Umm Atiya, may Allah be pleased with her, that we were ordered to take young girls and menstruating women along with us on Eid so that they too may participate in the prayers of the Muslims. (Don't join the prayer, just attend the prayer.) (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"390","Hazrat Ibn Umar (RA) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) used to lead the Eid prayer before the sermon with Abu Bakr and Umar (RA). (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"391","It was narrated from Hazrat Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, performed only two rak'ahs on the day of Eid. (It has been narrated by all seven)."
"392","It was narrated from Hazrat Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, performed the Eid prayer without a call to prayer or Iqamah. (Narrated by Abu Dawud and its original is in Bukhari.)"
"393","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, he stated that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not offer any prayer before the Eid prayer. (It was narrated by Ibn Majah with a hasan chain of transmission.)"
"394","It was narrated from Hazrat Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) that the Prophet (PBUH) used to go to the Eidgah for Eid-ul-Fitr and Eid-ul-Adha and the first thing he would start with was prayer. After performing the prayer, he would turn his back and stand in front of the people, and the people would be sitting in their rows at that time. (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"395","Hazrat Amr bin Shuaib narrates from his father and he from his grandfather, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \There are seven takbirs in the first rak'ah of the Eid al-Fitr prayer and five in the second rak'ah.\"" In both rak'ats"," the recitation is after the takbirat."""
"396","It was narrated from Hazrat Abu Waqid Laithi that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite Surah Q and Surah Iqtarbat-e-Sa'at in the prayers of Eid-ul-Adha and Eid-ul-Fitr. (Narrated by Muslim.)"
"397","It was narrated from Hazrat Jabir that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to change his route to and from the place of Eid on the day of Eid. (It was narrated by Bukhari. And in Abu Dawud, it is also narrated from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him)."
"398","It was narrated from Hazrat Anas that when the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to Madinah, the people of Madinah were scheduled for two days of sports. He said: \Allah has given you two days in exchange for these two days that are better than them: one is the day of Eid al-Adha and the other is the day of Eid al-Fitr.\"""""
"399","Hazrat Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) states that it is Sunnah to walk towards the Eidgah. (It has been narrated by Tirmidhi and has been classified as Hasan.)"
"400","It was narrated from Hazrat Abu Huraira that on one occasion it rained on the day of Eid, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allaah be upon him) led him in the Eid prayer in the mosque. (It was narrated by Abu Dawud with a weak chain of transmission.)"
"401","It was narrated from Hazrat Mugheera bin Shuba, that during the reign of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), there was an eclipse of the sun on the day of the death of Ibrahim (may Allah be pleased with him), so people said that the eclipse was due to the death of Ibrahim. On this, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Shams and Qamar are two of the signs of Allah.\"" They do not perceive the eclipse because of the death or life of anyone. So when you see them in this state"," pray to Allah Almighty and pray until it (the sun) becomes clear (the eclipse opens)\"" (Bukhari and Muslim) and in a tradition of Bukhari: \""Continue praying until it becomes bright.\"" \""Go away.\"""""
"402","It was narrated from Hazrat Aisha that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited aloud in the eclipse prayer and performed four ruku's and four prostrations in two rak'ahs. (Bukhari and Muslim. These words are from Muslim) and in a hadith of Muslim: He sent a preacher who used to preach [Al-Salaatu Jami’a] “She who collects the prayer.”"
"403","It was narrated from Hazrat Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, that there was an eclipse of the sun during the blessed period of the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace. He performed the Qasuf prayer and stayed in it for a long time, equivalent to the recitation of Surah Baqarah. Then he bowed too long, then he raised his head (standing up from bowing), then he made the qiyaam longer, but less than the first qiyaam. Then performed a long ruku but less than the first ruku. Then he prostrated (after that), then he stayed for a long time, and it was a little shorter than the first stay. Then performed a long ruku which was a little shorter than the first ruku. Then he raised his blessed head (by bowing) and made a long stay which was a little shorter than the first stay. After that, he performed another long ruku which was a little shorter than the first ruku. Then he raised his blessed head (by bowing), then he prostrated, then (finally) returned the salutation, and (by this time) the sun had risen. Then he preached to the people. (Bukhari and Muslim - these words are Bukhari's) It is in a hadith of Muslim: When he prayed on the occasion of a solar eclipse, he performed eight bows between the four prostrations. Hazrat Ali (RA) also has a similar tradition. And there is also a tradition of Muslim from Hazrat Jabir (RA): He performed six bows (Ruku') with four prostrations. Ruku and two Sajdahs were performed in the first rak'at and likewise in the second rak'at."
"404","It was narrated from Hazrat Ibn Abbas (RA) that whenever there was a strong wind, the Prophet (PBUH) would sit on his knees and say (in the presence of God): “God! Make it (the wind) a mercy and do not make it a punishment.” (Narrated by both Shafi’i and Tabrani)."
"405","This hadith has also been narrated from Hazrat Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, that because of the earthquake, he prayed with four prostrations and six bows, and he said that the prayers of the divine verses are recited in the same way. (It has been narrated by Bayhaqi. And Imam Shafi'i has mentioned a similar tradition from Hazrat Ali bin Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, but it does not contain the last words of the tradition.)"
"406","It was narrated from Hazrat Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out for prayer while remaining modest, giving up adornment, showing humility, walking slowly, and making loud cries and supplications, and he led the people in two rak'ahs of prayer like the Eid prayer. He did not deliver a sermon like yours. (It has been narrated by all five and has been declared authentic by Tirmidhi, Abu Awana and Ibn Hibban.)"
"407","It was narrated from Hazrat Aisha that the people complained to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that the rain had stopped, so he ordered the pulpit (to be taken away). He promised the people a day that they should all come out. Then he came out when the edge of the sun appeared. He sat on the pulpit and glorified and glorified Allah. Then he said: \All praise is due to Allah"," the Lord of the Universe"," the Most Merciful"," the Most Merciful.\"" The day is the owner of reward. There is no god but Allah. He does what he wants. God! You are Allah"," there is no other god but You. He is rich and we are poor and needy. Send down the rain of mercy on us. Whatever You send down upon us"," make it a strength for us and a means for a time. After that"," he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised both his blessed hands so that they gradually rose up and he engaged in supplication until the whiteness of his armpits began to be seen. Then he stood with his back to the people (Qiblah) and turned over his cloak while his hands were raised up. Then he turned his face to the people and came down from the minbar and prayed two rak'ahs. At that moment"," Allah Almighty sent a change"," it thundered"," flashed"," then started raining. (It was narrated by Abu Dawud and called Gharib"," and its chain of transmission is excellent. ) In Sahih Bukhari"," there is a story of changing the cloak in the narration of Hazrat Abdullah bin Zayd (RA). And it is in this hadith: Then he turned towards the qiblah and continued to pray"," then he offered two rak'ahs of prayer and recited aloud in them. And it is in the tradition of Abu Ja'far Baqir's messenger in Darqutni that he turned his cloak over so that the famine would also turn over in the same way."""
"408","It was narrated from Hazrat Anas that a man entered the mosque on Friday. He said: O Messenger of Allah! Property (cattle) has been killed and traffic routes have been blocked. Pray to Allah to send rain on us. At the same time, he raised his hands and prayed: \God! Hear our cry from the rain. God! Please shower our prayers with mercy. O Allah! Please accept our prayers with the rain of mercy.” Then he narrated the entire hadith. It also mentions the prayer to stop the rain. (Bukhari and Muslim)"""
"409","It was narrated on the authority of Hazrat Anas that during the time of Hazrat Umar (RA), when the people were suffering from famine, he would ask for rain through the prayer of Hazrat Abbas bin Abdul Muttalib (RA) and would pray like this: “O Allah! We used to ask You for rain through the prayer of Your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and He used to bless us with rain. Now we ask for rain in your presence (through the prayer of the uncle of your Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace). (As a result of the acceptance of this supplication) they would be watered with rain. (Narrated by Bukhari.)"
"410","This hadith has also been narrated from Anas (RA) that once we were with the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) when it started to rain. So he removed the cloth from his body until the rain began to fall on his body and he said: \It has just come from my Lord.\"" (Narrated by Muslim)."""
"411","Hazrat Aisha (RA) narrated that when the Prophet (PBUH) saw the rain, he used to pray like this: “O Allah! Make this rain profitable.” (Narrated by Bukhari and Muslim.)"
"412","It was narrated from Hazrat Saad (RA) that the Prophet (PBUH) prayed for rain: “O God! Cover us with a cloud that is deep layer by layer, crackling, raining heavily, shining and thundering, then it will rain on us with small drops, very fine drops and heavy rain. O Lord of greatness and honor!\""413""","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Huraira, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \When Hazrat Sulaiman"," peace be upon him"," went out to ask for rain"," he saw an ant lying on its back with its legs raised towards the sky"," which was saying in the presence of the Almighty God: God! We are also one of your creations and are not exempt from your rain. Hearing this"," Hazrat Sulaiman (peace be upon him) said: Let's go back. You have been watered by the rain thanks to the supplication of others."""
"414","It was narrated from Anas (RA) that when the Prophet (PBUH) prayed for rain, he pointed to the sky with the backs of both his palms. (Narrated by Muslim.)"
"415","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Amr Ash'ari, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \There will definitely be some nations in my ummah who will consider adultery and silk as halal.\"""""
"416","It was narrated from Hazrat Hudhayfah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us to eat and drink in gold and silver vessels, to wear fine and thick silk and to sit on it. (Narrated by Bukhari.)"
"417","Hazrat Umar (RA) narrated that the Messenger of Allah (SAW) forbade wearing silk except for two or three or four inches of space. (Bukhari and Muslim. The words are by Muslim.)"
"418","Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted Hazrat Abd al-Rahman bin Awf and Zubayr bin Al-Awam (may Allah be pleased with him) to wear silk shirts while traveling because they had itching. (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"419","It was narrated from Hazrat Ali bin Abi Talib (RA) that the Prophet (PBUH) gave me a silk-striped Hala (pair). When I went out wearing it, I saw signs of anger and displeasure on your face, Anwar, so I tore it and distributed it among my (relative) women. (Bukhari and Muslim. These words are from Muslim.)"
"420","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Gold and silk have been made lawful for the women of my Ummah and forbidden for the men.\"""""
"421","On the authority of Hazrat Imran bin Hussain, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Allah"," the Most High"," likes that when He bestows a reward on one of His servants"," he sees the effect of this blessing on him.\"" (Narrated by Bayhaqi)."""
"422","Hazrat Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the wearing of clothes made of \Qis\"" (city) and yellow colored clothes. (Narrated by Muslim.)"""
"423","It was narrated from Hazrat Abdullah bin Amr that the Prophet saw two yellow clothes on my body and said: \Did your mother order you to wear these?\"" (Narrated by Muslim)."""
"424","It was narrated from Hazrat Asmaa bint Abi Bakr (may Allah be pleased with her) that she took out a robe of the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him) which had a border of striped silk on the collar, sleeves and chalk (chest bands). (It was narrated by Abu Dawud and its original is in Muslim.) Muslim has narrated so much that it was in the custody of Hazrat Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) when she died, I took it into my possession. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to adorn it. We wash it and give it to the sick and pray for healing. Al-Bukhari has narrated this addition in Al-Adab Al-Mufard that the Prophet (peace be upon him) used to wear it on the arrival of delegations and for Friday prayers."
